STEPS TO FLOW:
_______________

Step 1: launch 2 EC2 instance.
(one is for jenkins master and another one is for Slave nodes)

Step 2: In one instance install jenkins
Pre-requisites to install Jenkins:
Java

Step 3: create ssh key one public and one private.

Step 4: Before creating ssh key u need to change path.
Path change command:
#sudo su - jenkins
ssh key generating Command:
#ssk-keygen

Step 5: Copy ssh pub key and paste it in slave instance.

Step 6: login into the slave machine. Create root directory for jenkins.

Step 7: add user
Command: 
#sudo adduser jenkins
#sudo mkdir -p /hoe/jenkins/.shh
#sudo nano /home/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys

Step 8: in authorized_keys file paste ssh public key, where we copied in master machine.

Step 9: Provide permissions for user and ssh key file path.
Commands: 
#sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins /home/jenkins/.ssh
#sudo chmod 700 /home/jenkins/.ssh
#sudo chmod 600 /home/jenkins/.ssh/authorized_keys

Step 10: Test the connection from master (Jenkins) to slave machine.
command :
#ssh jenkins@<slave ip>

Step 11: Login into the Jenkins Dashboard.

Step 12: Create Node in jenkins.
Navigate to manage jenkins -> nodes -> Create Node.
Name: give name for agent sample (slave)
Typr: Permanent Agent
Description: optional
No.of executore: 1 or 2 based on server cpu and memory capacity.
Remote root directory: /home/jenkins
Lable: give something to identify agent. (slave)
usage: use this node as much as possible.
Launch Method: launch agent via ssh
  host: ip of slave server 
  credentials: add credentials 
    kind : ssh username with private key
    id : anything to identify easily
    description: anything to identify easily
    username: ubuntu
    private key: copy private key from master node and paste here.
    save
  Host Key Verification Strategy: Non verifying Verification Strategy
  Availability: Keep this agent online as much as possible
  save

Step 13: Now check the node status, whether syn or not.

Step 14: Crate new Job.
Step 15: in job configuration in general select Restrict where this project can be run
in lable give node lable.


**** If jenkins showing Perission denied error means ****
Give jenkins user permissions ..
example:
/var/www/sruthi/websites/ ------------> this path does not having permission means 
# sudo chown -R jenkins:jenkins /var/www/sruthi/websites/
now we can work on this path
